# .gitignore — proposal/src/
#
# Template-owned; copier update keeps it current, and it ships only while the project keeps
# its binary records under the data root (DATA_STORE external). Leaving that store deletes it.
# No inline comments in this file: Git reads a # after a pattern as part of the pattern.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary records, filed under the data root
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scans, signed and received copies, issued PDFs and Word copies, images, audio and video
# live under the machine's data root, at this same path, each listed with its checksum in
# external.toml beside this file: file one with make files-add, never with git add. Every
# extension the data-root tool counts as a binary is ignored here, in any letter case. An
# ignore rule never untracks a file: a binary already in Git stays there until the owner
# moves it (make files-plan).

# Documents
*.[pP][dD][fF]
*.[dD][oO][cC]
*.[dD][oO][cC][xX]
*.[xX][lL][sS]
*.[xX][lL][sS][xX]
*.[pP][pP][tT]
*.[pP][pP][tT][xX]
*.[oO][dD][tT]
*.[oO][dD][sS]
*.[oO][dD][pP]
*.[zZ][iI][pP]
*.7[zZ]
*.[tT][aA][rR]
*.[gG][zZ]
*.[eE][mM][lL]
*.[mM][sS][gG]

# Photos
*.[pP][nN][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
*.[tT][iI][fF]
*.[tT][iI][fF][fF]
*.[hH][eE][iI][cC]
*.[wW][eE][bB][pP]
*.[gG][iI][fF]
*.[pP][sS][dD]
*.[bB][mM][pP]
*.[dD][nN][gG]
*.[eE][xX][rR]

# Audio
*.[mM][pP]3
*.[wW][aA][vV]
*.[fF][lL][aA][cC]
*.[mM]4[aA]
*.[oO][gG][gG]
*.[aA][aA][cC]
*.[aA][iI][fF]
*.[aA][iI][fF][fF]
*.[oO][pP][uU][sS]
*.[pP][cC][mM]

# Video
*.[mM][pP]4
*.[mM][oO][vV]
*.[mM][kK][vV]
*.[wW][eE][bB][mM]
*.[mM][xX][fF]
*.[mM]4[vV]
*.[mM][tT][sS]
*.[mM]2[tT][sS]
*.[aA][vV][iI]
*.[bB][rR][aA][wW]
*.[rR]3[dD]

# The data-root tool's temporary copy while it files a file
*.syntek-tmp

# Never ignored: the manifest that lists what is filed, and the folder's README
!external.toml
!README.md
